---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy policy — Reeltotranscript" description="How Reeltotranscript handles sign-in, uploaded clips, transcripts and daily usage." canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 py-16 leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold">Privacy policy</h1>
    <section class="my-6"><h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Sign-in and verification</h2><p>Google handles sign-in. We check your verified account and store a hash of its account ID to enforce the daily limit. A secure session cookie expires after seven days. Cloudflare Turnstile checks transcription requests.</p></section>
    <section class="my-6"><h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Media and transcripts</h2><p>The service receives your link or uploaded media and processes it on our server. Temporary media is removed when processing finishes. A finished transcript is available to your account for 15 minutes and then cleared from server memory on the next cleanup pass. Save your copy before leaving.</p></section>
    <section class="my-6"><h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Usage and preferences</h2><p>The service keeps job IDs, account hashes and usage records for about two days. Short-lived request counters help limit abuse. Your browser stores the theme preference and the current job ID so you can refresh during processing.</p></section>
    <section class="my-6"><h2 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Providers</h2><p>Google and Cloudflare receive information needed for authentication, traffic delivery and abuse prevention. For a link submission, the video platform receives a request from our server.</p></section>
    <a class="underline" href="mailto:hello@reeltotranscript.com">hello@reeltotranscript.com</a>
  </article>
</Layout>
